 "starter": "from typing import Optional\n\n\nclass FirmwareVersion:\n    \"\"\"An immutable firmware version such as 24.1.3 or 24.1.3-rc.2 (fields: major, minor, patch, rc).\"\"\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def parse(cls, text: str) -> \"FirmwareVersion\":\n        pass\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Provided \u2014 keep this. The tests call exercise(texts): it parses each text with your class,\n# then sorts, de-duplicates and probes the class contract (repr, ==, <, immutability, subclassing).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List\n\n\ndef _outcome(action):\n    try:\n        return [\"ok\", action()]\n    except Exception as err:\n        return [\"raised\", \"AttributeError\" if isinstance(err, AttributeError) else type(err).__name__]\n\n\ndef _contract(v):\n    class Nightly(FirmwareVersion):\n        pass\n\n    def assign():\n        v.major = 99\n\n    nightly = Nightly.parse(str(v))\n    return {\n        \"repr\": repr(v),\n        \"equals_its_string\": v == str(v),\n        \"less_than_string\": _outcome(lambda: v < str(v)),\n        \"assign_major\": _outcome(assign)[0] + \":\" + str(v.major),\n        \"reparsed_equal_and_same_hash\": [FirmwareVersion.parse(str(v)) == v,\n                                         hash(FirmwareVersion.parse(str(v))) == hash(v)],\n        \"subclass_parse\": [type(nightly).__name__, repr(nightly)],\n        \"fields\": [v.major, v.minor, v.patch, v.rc],\n    }\n\n\ndef exercise(texts: List[str]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    versions, invalid = [], []\n    for text in texts:\n        try:\n            versions.append(FirmwareVersion.parse(text))\n        except ValueError:\n            invalid.append(text)\n    return {\n        \"canonical\": [str(v) for v in versions],\n        \"invalid\": invalid,\n        \"sorted\": [str(v) for v in sorted(versions)],\n        \"distinct\": len(set(versions)),\n        \"latest\": str(max(versions)) if versions else None,\n        \"contract\": _contract(versions[0]) if versions else None,\n    }\n",
 "compare": "exact",
 "notes": "Write FirmwareVersion with fields major, minor, patch and rc (an int, or None for a release). parse(text) strips surrounding whitespace, then accepts exactly MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH with an optional -rc.N suffix, where every number is one or more ASCII digits 0-9 (leading zeros allowed, so 1.02.3 equals 1.2.3); anything else raises ValueError. Versions are immutable, hashable and equal by value. Ordering is numeric, and 1.2.3-rc.N sorts before 1.2.3; comparing with a non-version with < raises TypeError, and == with a string is just False. str(v) is canonical (24.1.3-rc.2) and repr(v) is ClassName('24.1.3-rc.2') using the actual class name, and parse called on a subclass returns that subclass. exercise is provided.",
